Exp-12a:FileReader
Aim: To write a Java program to read data from a file using FileReader.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Import the java.io package.
3. Create a FileReader object.
4. Open the file using FileReader.
5. Read the characters from the file.
6. Display the file contents.
7. Close the file.
8. Stop the program.

Program:
File name: FileReaderExample.java
import java.io.*;

public class FileReaderExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            FileReader fr = new FileReader("sample.txt");

            int i;

            while ((i = fr.read()) != -1) {
                System.out.print((char)i);
            }

            fr.close();
        }
        catch (IOException e) {
            System.out.println(e);
        }
    }
}


